 "summary": "An amber caution: an overheat is detected near the hot air ducts in one wing. Switch the affected engine bleed OFF, shut the crossbleed and switch wing anti-ice OFF, so the crew must avoid icing conditions. For a left wing leak, also switch the APU bleed OFF if it has not closed. The STATUS lists the engine bleed, the pack on that side and wing anti-ice as inoperative.",
